# Ancient Trees of Ireland — Cursor guardrails

Read AGENTS.md and current data pipeline documentation before changing the map or source data. Canonical records are in public/data/trees.json; scripts and validation requirements are listed in AGENTS.md.

- Treat public register, FOI/AIE, heritage and land-boundary records as evidence, not automatically verified facts. Preserve provenance, source URL/document reference, date, confidence and any uncertainty in coordinate placement.
- Do not fabricate tree coordinates, protected status or council responses. Prefer verified site-level pins over county/town centroids; flag uncertain records instead of upgrading confidence without evidence.
- For imported data, keep raw source separate from normalized fields, record transformations and detect duplicates/contradictions. Avoid overwriting manually verified records without a reviewed reconciliation.
- Use existing scripts, including npm run data:apply-placement and npm run data:audit when coordinates change; choose lint, typecheck, build and Playwright checks based on the work. Do not claim a check passed unless executed.
- Avoid network geocoding loops that violate Nominatim rate limits; use cached/reproducible outputs and deterministic validation where possible.
- Never publish private FOI contacts or personally identifying data extracted from responses without authorization.
- Create PRs with data-change counts, source evidence, validation results and unresolved clusters. No production deploy, merge or bulk overwrite without explicit approval.
